# Accepted Trivy misconfiguration findings. Each one is a deliberate decision, not an oversight.

# KSV-0011 (LOW) CPU limits: not set on purpose. CPU is compressible: a limit only throttles the
# JVM (slow start-up, latency) without protecting the node. Requests guarantee fair scheduling;
# memory limits, which do matter, are enforced by the require-resources Kyverno policy.
KSV-0011

# KSV-0020 / KSV-0021 (LOW) UID/GID above 10000: PostgreSQL (70) and Keycloak (1000) run as the
# non-root users their images were built for. Pod Security "restricted" already forbids root.
KSV-0020
KSV-0021

# KSV-0125 (MEDIUM) "untrusted registry": Trivy only knows a generic list. This lab enforces its
# own allow-list (postgres, quay.io/keycloak/, lab.local/) with the restrict-image-registries
# Kyverno policy, at admission time.
KSV-0125

# DS-0026 (LOW) HEALTHCHECK: the headercheck image runs as a short-lived Job, not a service;
# Kubernetes ignores Dockerfile HEALTHCHECKs anyway and uses probes instead.
DS-0026
